# shared_dsp.py is duplicated between this repo and the bridge, and the copy is
# verified by SHA-256 of the WHOLE FILE (tests/test_shared_dsp_sync.py). Git's
# core.autocrlf is `true` on the machine this was written on, which rewrites every
# line ending on checkout — so a fresh clone would hash differently from the repo it
# was cloned from, and the divergence check would go red for a reason that has nothing
# whatsoever to do with the DSP. Pinning these files to LF is what makes "byte for
# byte" mean the same thing in both checkouts.
#
# Both layouts are listed so this file can be copied to the bridge unchanged: the
# listener owns listener/shared_dsp.py, the bridge carries host/shared_dsp.py.
listener/shared_dsp.py         text eol=lf
host/shared_dsp.py             text eol=lf
tests/test_shared_dsp_sync.py  text eol=lf
